{
  "$comment": [
    "GOLDEN VECTORS — the arithmetic contract for the What-if Simulator.",
    "",
    "Every expected value in this file was computed BY HAND from SPEC.md before",
    "simulate.ts existed. That is the whole point: the engine is validated against",
    "numbers derived independently of the code, not against its own output.",
    "",
    "RULE (SPEC §12): when a vector fails, verify the new number by hand before",
    "touching this file. Updating vectors to match new output is exactly how a",
    "financial engine silently becomes wrong.",
    "",
    "`expect` keys are dotted paths into SimulationResult. Money is rounded to 2dp",
    "at result-construction time; internal maths runs at full float precision.",
    "Derived non-money values are rounded to 4dp."
  ],

